    <dcterms:title>Watch and ward</dcterms:title>
    <pgterms:marc260>  $aBoston :$bHoughton, Osgood and Company, $c1878.</pgterms:marc260>
    <dcterms:description>First published in the Atlantic monthly, 1871.</dcterms:description>
    <dcterms:description>Wikipedia page about this book: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Watch_and_Ward</dcterms:description>
    <pgterms:marc508>Al Haines</pgterms:marc508>
    <pgterms:marc520>"Watch and Ward" by Henry James is a novel first published as a serial in 1871. When wealthy Roger Lawrence adopts twelve-year-old Nora Lambert out of remorse, he secretly plans to marry her once she matures. But as Nora blossoms into a beautiful young woman, she finds herself drawn to other men, complicating Roger's designs. This melodramatic tale, which James later disowned, traces a controversial guardianship that transforms into romantic pursuit, complete with villains, rivals, and a climactic rescue in New York City. (This is an automatically generated summary.)</pgterms:marc520>
    <pgterms:marc904>https://archive.org/details/watchward1878jame</pgterms:marc904>
    <pgterms:marc905>20231207164507james</pgterms:marc905>
    <pgterms:marc906>1878</pgterms:marc906>
    <pgterms:marc907>us</pgterms:marc907>
    <pgterms:marc908>Reading ease score: 82.5 (6th grade). Easy to read.</pgterms:marc908>
